<topic id="GUID-D550E81B-3CAA-4B4E-944E-710E2C66E757" xml:lang="en-US"> 
  <title>Early Power Management Configuration</title> 
  <body> 
    <p> Prior to this platform, power management BIOS configurations did not take effect until BIOS_RST_CPL is set. Before this phase, the SOC runs at safe voltages/FIVR's and does not have efficient power delivery configuration, which might require BIOS workaround for thermal issues during Intel® MRC. In this platform, we are now adding new BIOS-PCODE sync (Early VR Done) where PM flows starts. 
    </p> 
    <p> BIOS shall program Early VR done to message PCODE via Mailbox for indicating Pre-MRC VR/PM configuration settings. 
    </p> 
    <section id="SECTION_F9C217E64A57459A934D6226130F4F72"> 
      <title>Protocol</title> 
      <p> 
      <ol id="OL_30393DFC67C9421C9686D59FEE1FCC73"> 
        <li id="LI_CEEC5405914141E58706CA99F417A4A5"> BIOS configures early PD/PM configuration 
        </li> 
        <li id="LI_342B4EEE38E2456989580B8961971980"> BIOS notifies punit through a mailbox that configuration is done 
          <ol id="OL_D23B59FBE7CC4F8EA4207AC350921662"> 
            <li id="LI_5288162F2E3642669610CDD5FE6500A9"> Write BIOS-&gt;punit mailbox command EARLY_PM_CONFIG (param1=0, Param2=0, data = 0, run/busy=1) 
            </li> 
            <li id="LI_3E9914CF59464A519B0F623061FDB0E5"> BIOS will poll and wait for MAILBOX_INTERFACE.RUN_BUSY = 0 
            </li> 
            <li id="LI_66D96B4B4CC4477AB7832D6737CB3868"> If return data = 1 - request is granted - pcode has acked the request. 
            </li> 
            <li id="LI_920BAA0CAA054CA69900359BE312E5C6"> If return data = 0 - request in progress. BIOS needs to re-issue the mailbox command to check if pcode is done. 
            </li> 
          </ol> 
        </li> 
        <li id="LI_79B48E2CBFD4439EAE0F57D346F0B669"> PCODE will perform necessary actions to ack the BIOS request, for example - enable early power management once done, pcode will indicate it by replying to the mailbox command with 'Request granted'. 
        </li> 
      </ol> 
      </p> 
      <table id="TABLE_F78DDB57EEC0489999D6EC4E631F2547"> 
      <title> New BIOS Pcode Mailbox Command for EARLY_PM_CONFIG</title> 
      <tgroup cols="2"> 
        <colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="*" /> 
        <colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="*" /> 
        <thead> 
          <row> 
            <entry> Field 
            </entry> 
            <entry> Value 
            </entry> 
          </row></thead> 
        <tbody> 
          <row> 
            <entry> MAILBOX_INTERFACE.Command 
            </entry> 
            <entry> EARLY_PM_CONFIG (opcode 0x46) 
            </entry> 
          </row> 
          <row> 
            <entry> MAILBOX_INTERFACE.Param1 
            </entry> 
            <entry> 0 (reserved for future) 
            </entry> 
          </row> 
          <row> 
            <entry> MAILBOX_INTERFACE.Param2 
            </entry> 
            <entry> 0 (reserved for future) 
            </entry> 
          </row> 
          <row> 
            <entry> MAILBOX_INTERFACE.RUN_BUSY 
            </entry> 
            <entry> run/busy value 
            </entry> 
          </row> 
          <row> 
            <entry> MAILBOX_DATA 
            </entry> 
            <entry> 0 (reserved for future) 
            </entry> 
          </row> 
        </tbody> 
      </tgroup> 
      </table> 
      <table id="TABLE_F7ED19BA586745419E009CC7319C76DD"> 
      <title>Response</title> 
      <tgroup cols="2"> 
        <colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="*" /> 
        <colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="*" /> 
        <thead> 
          <row> 
            <entry> Field 
            </entry> 
            <entry> Value 
            </entry> 
          </row></thead> 
        <tbody> 
          <row> 
            <entry> MAILBOX_INTERFACE.RESPONSE 
            </entry> 
            <entry> 0 
            </entry> 
          </row> 
          <row> 
            <entry> MAILBOX_DATA 
            </entry> 
            <entry> 1: Request granted. 0: Request in progress (need to retry until request is granted) 
            </entry> 
          </row> 
        </tbody> 
      </tgroup> 
      </table> 
    </section> 
    <section id="SECTION_444B15B776A24D7A972ACDAA3D0E6BEE"> 
